{
  "_about": "The illustration board's templates, as the model sees them (core/irene/board.py builds its catalogue from this; one line each) and as the tests draw them (every example is rendered and checked by hud/tests/board.verify.mjs). Each template is one module in hud/src/board/templates/<name>.ts, found automatically; a new template is that module plus one entry here. 'required' lists the arguments core checks are present before the drawing is sent; the HUD then checks everything exactly and draws nothing if it can't. 'hint' is how a drawing request names the template (brain adds it to the prompt's Now section, the way act-outs are named). 'retired' templates are no longer offered to the model (Round 8: she composes explanations herself, core/irene/drawing.py) but still draw if sent.",
  "templates": [
    {
      "name": "chessboard",
      "family": "chess",
      "args": "moves (SAN list or PGN text, played one by one - an opening is ALWAYS its moves), fen?, title?, highlight? [squares], arrows? [[from,to]], flip?",
      "when": "a position, a move, any opening (write out its moves) or a game",
      "required": [],
      "example": {
        "template": "chessboard",
        "title": "Ruy Lopez",
        "moves": [
          "e4",
          "e5",
          "Nf3",
          "Nc6",
          "Bb5"
        ],
        "arrows": [
          [
            "b5",
            "c6"
          ]
        ]
      },
      "hint": "[rnbqkpRNBQKP1-8]{1,8}(/[rnbqkpRNBQKP1-8]{1,8}){7}|chess|opening|gambit|defen[cs]e|sicilian|ruy lopez|najdorf|london system|italian game|indian|caro-?kann|slav|nimzo|grunfeld|catalan|scotch|vienna|petrov|english opening|dutch defen[cs]e|fen|checkmate|scholar'?s mate|fool'?s mate|\\b1\\.\\s*[a-h][1-8]|\\be4\\b|\\bd4\\b",
      "retired": "Round 8: not offered to the model (her spec's chess helper); still drawn if sent"
    },
